1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,176
I stole a fake coat and left the real
one. Jason thought rain had ruined

2
00:00:06,176 --> 00:00:07,000
my judgment.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,125
The real coat had a perfect label. The
fake had crooked stitching and a

4
00:00:13,125 --> 00:00:14,000
sagging hem.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,444
Our buyer said the fee was inside a
pocket. Both pockets were empty, Jason

6
00:00:19,444 --> 00:00:21,000
reached for his phone.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,053
I checked the claim ticket instead. It
listed alterations, not storage,

8
00:00:25,053 --> 00:00:28,000
and charged for replacing six feet of
lining.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,789
Someone had stitched our money into the
hem. The bad label made sure

10
00:00:32,789 --> 00:00:35,000
nobody would steal it by accident.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,533
I took the seam apart with the booth's
scissors. Six bundles slid onto the

12
00:00:41,533 --> 00:00:42,000
counter.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,353
Jason counted the fee twice. I kept the
coat, because its supplier had

14
00:00:47,353 --> 00:00:49,000
taste in hiding places.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,789
Back outside, he offered his jacket. I
told him mine had already earned

16
00:00:53,789 --> 00:00:56,000
more tonight than either of us.
